From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: B Honey <9922368+Mhsbrian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/28] nvk/android: copy VRAM swapchain images to the window
 buffer with the copy engine

0021 renders a swapchain image whose window buffer is linear into a
tiled image in VRAM, and copies it into the window buffer in the release
submission with vkCmdCopyImage2().  On a graphics queue NVK runs that
copy as a 3D draw (nvk_cmd_copy_image_meta()), whose writes reach the
window buffer in system memory over PCIe.  On the G14 (RTX 5070 Ti
Laptop on a PCIe 4.0 x8 link) the copy is most of a light ANGLE frame:
glmark2's clear scene (RGB565) takes 0.582 ms a frame at 2073x1224 and
1.147 ms at 2880x1800, about 9.4 GB/s plus 40 us, and its build scene
runs at 1700 fps.  Rendering into the window buffer instead
(NVK_ANB_VRAM=0), which for a depth-buffered app means NVK's tiled
shadow and its copy-engine copy-out (nvk_linear_render_copy()), runs
build at 2608 fps, 13.2 GB/s or more.  (ANAL-351)

Record the copy with nvk_cmd_copy_image_ce(), the copy-engine path NVK
takes on queues without graphics or compute.  The barriers around it
stay: the first waits for idle, and NVK's switch from the 3D to the
copy engine's subchannel is a wait for idle as well.

Public sources: Mesa 26.2.5 src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_meta.c
(nvk_CmdCopyImage2, nvk_meta_image_copy_gfx_supported), nvk_cmd_copy.c
(nvk_cmd_copy_image_ce, nvk_linear_render_copy, nouveau_copy_rect),
nvk_cmd_draw.c (nvk_rendering_linear,
nvk_image_plane_aligned_for_linear_attachment) and nvk_cmd_buffer.c
(nvk_cmd_flush_wait_dep).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_android.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_android.c b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_android.c
index 77c1bfc..fae53c4 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_android.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_android.c
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 
 #include "nvk_private.h"
 
+#include "nvk_cmd_buffer.h"
 #include "nvk_device.h"
 #include "nvk_device_memory.h"
 #include "nvk_entrypoints.h"
@@ -528,7 +529,14 @@ nvk_android_anb_vram_copy_cmd(struct nvk_device *dev, struct nvk_image *image,
       .regionCount = 1,
       .pRegions = &region,
    };
-   disp->CmdCopyImage2(cmd, &copy);
+   /* With the copy engine.  On a graphics queue vkCmdCopyImage2() copies
+    * with a 3D draw, whose writes into the linear window buffer in system
+    * memory are slower over PCIe than the copy engine's: on the G14, about
+    * 9.4 GB/s against 13 GB/s or more for the copy-engine copy-out of NVK's
+    * tiled shadow (nvk_linear_render_copy()).  The barriers above and below
+    * apply to it as to any transfer.
+    */
+   nvk_cmd_copy_image_ce(nvk_cmd_buffer_from_handle(cmd), &copy);
 
    const VkImageMemoryBarrier2 after[2] = {{
       .sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_IMAGE_MEMORY_BARRIER_2,
